  <text>
    <body>
      <p>Bouverie Place is a lane off the west side of <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref>, near its south end. In 1879 the directory lists the turn into Bouverie Place just before Alma Street.</p>
      <p>It is first listed in the directories in 1879 and last in 1915. It had at most five listings, all of them houses.</p>
      <div>
        <head>Along the street</head>
        <p>In the Bouverie Street listings the turn comes between Nos 11 and 13 in 1879, and between Nos 19 and 21 in 1900.</p>
      </div>
    </body>
